    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that feels like just a way to distract myself, u know? like, a cup of coffee or a song doesn't actually change the fact that we're just accidental biological matter floating in nothingness. it's like trying to put a tiny band-aid on a massive, gaping wound. the more i think about the scale of it all, the more those \"small moments\" feel almost insulting. like, why bother pretending they matter when the end result is always just... nothing?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
